-- title:
--   Local Artin map computes carry classes on an enlarged layer
-- statement:
--   Let $E \subseteq F, F' \subseteq K$ be number fields with $K/E$, $F/E$, $F'/E$ Galois and $\mathrm{Gal}(K/E)$ commutative, and assume every element of $K$ lies in the $E$-subalgebra generated by the images of $F$ and $F'$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_E$ and $w_K$ one of $\mathcal{O}_K$ lying under $v$, and write $H$ for the decomposition subgroup [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.decomp E K wK`](def/NumberField_PlaceDecompositionAction.html#L82) of $K \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} K$ attached to the valuation subring of $w_K$, assumed commutative. Given monoid homomorphisms $\rho$, $\rho'$ from $H$ to the decomposition groups of $F$, $F'$ at the primes under $w_K$, each inducing the restriction of automorphisms to $F$, resp. $F'$, with $\rho'$ surjective, with $\rho' \sigma = 1$ exactly when $\sigma$ fixes the image of $F'$ pointwise, and with every element of the decomposition group of $K/F'$ at $w_K$ arising by restriction of scalars from some $\sigma \in H$ with $\rho' \sigma = 1$; assume further that the ramification index of the prime of $\mathcal{O}_{F'}$ under $w_K$ over the prime of $\mathcal{O}_E$ under it is $1$, and that $|\,$decomposition group of $F/E\,|$ divides $|\,$decomposition group of $F'/E\,|$. Let $q$ be a prime, $L_2$ a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside `PadicAlgCl q` carrying a faithful multiplicative semiring action of $H$ together with a compatible action on $L_2^\times$, and $\Phi_2 : K_{w_K} \simeq L_2$ a ring isomorphism; it is assumed that $H$ fixes the image of $\mathbb{Q}_q$, that the unit action is induced by the field action, and that $\Phi_2$ is $H$-equivariant. Let $K_0$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ in `PadicAlgCl q` which is a base for $L_2$ in the sense of [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsBase`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L13), namely $K_0 \le L_2$ and an element of $L_2$ lies in $K_0$ precisely when it is $H$-fixed, and let $u_2 \in H^2(H, L_2^\times)$ satisfy [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsLocalFundamentalClass`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L60). Let $\mathfrak{f}_K$ be a nonzero ideal of $\mathcal{O}_E$ admissible of degree $[K:E]$ in the sense that $v^{\,\mathrm{admissibleExpOfDegree}}$ divides $\mathfrak{f}_K$ at every prime whose chosen prime above has nontrivial inertia, and let $r_K$ be a homomorphism from the idèle units of $E$ to $\mathrm{Gal}(K/E)$ which is surjective, kills the principal idèles, has kernel exactly the principal idèles together with the image of the idelic norm of the base change $E \to K$, and satisfies $r_K(u) = \prod^{f}_{v} \mathrm{artinFrob}(E,K,v)^{\mathrm{placeOrd}(E)(\mathrm{projFin}(E)(u))(v)}$ for every $u$ which is an adjuster for $\mathfrak{f}_K$ relative to $1$. Let $\iota_v$ embed $E_v^\times$ into the idèle units with values trivial at the archimedean part and at every finite place other than $v$ and with $v$-component the given one, and let $f_E : E_v^\times \to H$ have underlying automorphism $r_K(\iota_v(z))$. Finally let $t \in H/\ker\rho$ be of finite order with every element of the quotient a power of $t$, let $a \in E_v^\times$, and let $b_2 \in L_2^\times$ have the same image in `PadicAlgCl q` as $\Phi_2$ applied to the image of $a$ under the semialgebra map $E_v \to K_{w_K}$, with $b_2$ invariant under $\ker\rho$, and assume the function $\mathrm{carryFun}(t)$ at $b_2$, formed in the $\ker\rho$-invariants quotient representation and equal to $b_2$ or $0$ according as the cyclic logarithms of the two arguments sum to at least $\mathrm{ord}(t)$ or not, is a $2$-cocycle. The conclusion is that there exists $m \in \mathbb{N}$ with $f_E(a) \equiv t^m$ in $H/\ker\rho$, and such that the inflation from $H/\ker\rho$ to $H$ of the degree-two class of this carry cocycle equals $(m \cdot |\ker\rho|) \cdot u_2$ in $H^2(H, L_2^\times)$.
--
--   This is the invariant form of Serre's axiomatic characterisation of the local reciprocity map, applied to the composite of the idelic Artin map of $K/E$ with the single-place embedding $E_v^\times \to \mathbb{I}_E$: the Frobenius and norm properties force $f_E$ to compute the carry class of every cyclic quotient of the decomposition group, here the quotient by $\ker\rho$ attached to the subextension $F$, with the unramified subextension $F'$ providing the overlayer datum. It feeds the computation of local coordinates and of the quotient by the order of the decomposition group in [`M4aHerbrand.exists_localCoordinate_carry_eq_zsmul_and_div_natCard_decomp_eq_of_idelicArtinMap`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_localCoordinate_carry_eq_zsmul_and_div_natCard_decomp_eq_of_idelicArtinMap).
